  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A string t1t2…tmt_1 t_2 \\ldots t_mt1​t2​…tm​ is called good if there is at most one position 1≤i&lt;m1\\le i &lt; m1≤i&lt;m such that ti≠ti+1t_i \\ne t_{i+1}ti​=ti+1​. For example `aaabb` and `zzz` are good strings; while `abc` and `ssdddssds` are not good.\n\nYou are given a string sss, consisting of lowercase English letters.\n\nFind the minimum kkk such that you can split sss into kkk good subsequences (a subsequence is not necessarily contiguous). Each character of sss should belong to exactly one of the kkk subsequences.\n\nIt can be shown that it is always possible to split sss into several subsequences this way.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line of the input contains a string sss.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single integer −-− the answer to the problem.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤∣s∣≤1061 \\le |s| \\le 10^{6}1≤∣s∣≤106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
